{
  "title": "02 Blender rigging tips",
  "sections": [
    {
      "02_01 Useful shortcuts": {
        "tags": [
          "tips"
        ],
        "key_concepts": [
          "The course is made of six chapters:",
          {
            "section": {
              "header": "Armature Modes",
              "content": [
                "When rigging and working with armature objects, you will be switching through three modes: [k]Pose[/k], [k]Edit[/k], and [k]Object[/k] modes. In the 3D view with the armature active:",
                [
                  "[k]CTRL-Tab[/k] = toggle pose mode",
                  "[k]Tab[/k] = toggle edit mode"
                ],
                {
                  "image": []
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "section": {
              "header": "Hiding",
              "content": [
                "Oftentimes you will want to hide bones you are working with. Whatever the context:",
                [
                  "[k]H[/k] : hide selected",
                  "[k]Shift-H[/k] : hide unselected",
                  "[k]Alt-H[/k] : unhide"
                ],
                {
                  "image": []
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "section": {
              "header": "Local Mode",
              "content": [
                "You can isolate the object you are working on in [k]Local Mode[/k]. Only the selected objects are shown and only in the current editor.",
                [
                  "[k]/[/k] : toggle local mode"
                ],
                {
                  "image": []
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "section": {
              "header": "Outliner",
              "content": [
                "The [k]Outliner[/k] is very helpful with enabling the selection and visibility restriction filters.",
                [
                  "[k]LMB[/k] : toggle restriction",
                  "[k]Shift-LMB[/k] : toggle restriction inside collection or to children",
                  "[k]CTRK-LMB[/k] : isolate"
                ],
                {
                  "image": []
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "section": {
              "header": "Box Selection",
              "content": [
                "Box selection, works in any editor and any mode. It is additive, so it will add more to the current selection each time it is used. Holding [k]Shift-LMB[/k] will make it a focus selection, only selecting items that fall into the current selection.",
                [
                  "[k]B[/k] : toggle restriction",
                  "[k]Shift-LMB[/k] : focus selection",
                  "[k]CTRK-LMB[/k] : isolate"
                ],
                {
                  "image": []
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}